title: file-manager panel
tags: Panel [[Panel types]]
kind: reference
aliases: file-manager files file-browser
summary: The disk, one directory at a time: which entries have a metarecord, which are left out and why, and the file operations of a file browser.

Open it with `panel:open here file-manager`
(<<key "panel:open here file-manager" "t m">>). It reads the disk itself and asks the
daemon only what the repository knows about the entries shown. So it lists a file
whether it is tracked or not, and it works with no repository at all, as a plain disk
browser.

!! The listing

One row per entry of the directory, sorted by name: a type icon, the name, and at the
right what the repository says about it. Two rows come first, as in a Unix listing:
`.`, the directory itself, and `..`, its parent. They make the directory's own
metarecord selectable — the repository root's included.

|!Mark |!Means |
|green name, `tracked` |the entry has a metarecord in the workspace's repository |
|`✓` and a green row |its metarecord is checked ([[Cross-panel selection]]) |
|`⊘`, `ignored` or `not watched` |left out on purpose: an `mf_ignore` pattern excludes it, or an `mf_watch = false` starts there; the tooltip names the pattern and the directory it is set on ([[Setting ignore patterns]]) |
|amber, `⏏ not mounted` |it sits on a volume that is not plugged in: unavailable, not deleted ([[Unmounted volumes in the GUI]]) |
|red, `internal` |the repository's `.metafolder/internal/`, which is never tracked ([[Repository layout on disk]]) |
|a number |watcher events under the entry since the repository was loaded, amber on a hot spot ([[Watch activity]]) |
|a number followed by `op` |operations the watcher wrote to the log for the entry — what those events cost |
|`⚠` after the name |the name holds bytes that are not text and is shown escaped ([[Tree names]]) |

An untracked entry of a directory that is not watched carries no mark: only the place
where an exclusion ''starts'' is marked, or a fresh repository would mark every row.
Without a repository nothing is marked.

Dot-entries are hidden until ''hidden files'' is checked
(<<key "file-manager:toggle hidden" Ctrl+h>>); `.` and `..` always show. ''by
activity'' (<<key "file-manager:toggle activity" "v a">>) puts the busiest
entries first, ''by operations'' (<<key "file-manager:toggle operations" "v o">>)
the ones the watcher wrote the most for; choosing one leaves the other.

The rows are drawn 200 at a time (`[page-size]`, [[GUI configuration]]), the next
ones when the scroll reaches the end; the footer gives `shown/total entries` and how
many metarecords are checked. A directory that cannot be read shows the reason in
place of its rows.

The marks follow the repository: they are read again whenever the daemon reports a
change. The ''entries'' are not watched — a file another program creates appears on
<<key "view:refresh self" "Ctrl+r">>, or after an operation of the panel's own.

!! Moving around

* <<key "cursor:next self" "↓">> / <<key "cursor:prev self" "↑">>, <<key "cursor:first self" Home>> / <<key "cursor:last self" End>> — move the cursor.
* <<key "file-manager:activate other" Enter>> — enter the directory under the cursor; on a file, or on `.` (the folder shown), show it in the [[viewer panel]] of the other slot (after `i` in place of this panel, after `b` in a new workspace).
* <<key "panel:open other metarecord-detail" Shift+Enter>> — show the entry's metarecord in the [[metarecord-detail panel]]; refused on an entry no metarecord records.
* The buttons at the start of a row ([[Opening a row]]) — `↘` on a folder enters it; `↗` on a file, or on `.`, shows it in the viewer panel; `ⓘ` in the detail panel (greyed when untracked).
* <<key "cursor:parent self" "Backspace or ←">>, or ''↑ up'' — the parent directory.
* <<key "cursor:root self" "Alt+Home">>, or the root button — the repository root; `/` when the workspace has no repository, and the button then reads ''root''.
* <<key "cursor:find self select" f>> — jump to an entry of this directory by name ([[Jumping to an entry]]).
* <<key "cursor:find self walk" "Shift+f">> — walk down by name: a directory found is entered and the question asked again, a file found is selected (`shift+Enter` stops on a directory).
* <<key "folder:open files here" "g d">> — a folder you use often and lately, from anywhere ([[Frecent folders]]). Each folder the panel goes into counts as a view of it.

Going back up — by ''↑ up'', the root button, their keys, or by entering `..` —
highlights the folder left (from the root, the top folder of the way left), so
the way back down is one Enter away. A command revealing a location says what to
highlight instead.

''constrain to repo root'' (<<key "file-manager:toggle root" "v r">>, checked at
first) keeps the browsing inside the repository: going above its root is refused, and
the root has no `..` row. Unchecked, the whole disk is reachable. Without a
repository the box is disabled.

!! The selection

The row under the cursor is the workspace's selection: its path, and its metarecord
when it has one. The panels beside it follow — a [[viewer panel]] previews the file,
[[metarecord-detail panel]] shows its fields ([[Cross-panel selection]]).

<<key "file-manager:select toggle" Space>> checks the metarecord of the row,
`file-manager:select all` every tracked entry of the directory, and
<<key "file-manager:select none" "Ctrl+Shift+a">> unchecks everything. The checked set is
the one [[metarecord-list panel]] gathers and the bulk operations act on. An untracked
entry has no metarecord to check, and the status bar says so.

!! Recording

''Add to DB'' (`file:record file-manager`) creates the metarecord of the entry under the
cursor with `mf_watch = false`: recorded, not watched ([[Recording a path]]). Parent
directories with no metarecord are named in a confirmation and created only if it is
accepted. The button is disabled on an entry that is already
tracked, outside the repository root or inside `internal/`.

!! File operations

These are the [[File commands]], run on this panel's files and folder.

|!Key |!Does |
|<<key "file:new self folder" Ctrl+Shift+n>>, <<key "file:new self file" Ctrl+n>> |create a folder, an empty file — the name is asked |
|<<key "file:rename self" F2>> |rename the entry |
|<<key "file:duplicate self" Ctrl+d>> |copy it beside itself, as `name copy.ext` |
|<<key "clipboard:copy self" Ctrl+c>>, <<key "clipboard:cut self" Ctrl+x>> |copy, cut the checked entries, or the one under the cursor ([[Generic panel commands]]) |
|<<key "file:paste self" Ctrl+v>> |paste into the directory shown |
|<<key "item:delete" Delete>> |send the entry to the trash, its metarecord with it ([[Deleting an item]]); with no repository, to the desktop's ([[The desktop trash]]) |

They act on the disk directly, not through the daemon. A tracked file that is renamed
or moved here keeps its metarecord once the [[Watcher]] has seen the move — a couple
of seconds later, and the `tracked` mark comes back by itself — or at the next
[[Reconcile]] where the directory is not watched.

Nothing is ever overwritten: creating or renaming onto a taken name is refused, and
a paste or a duplicate that would collide takes a ` copy` suffix (`foo copy.txt`,
`foo copy 2.txt`…). A directory is not pasted into itself or below.

The clipboard belongs to the GUI, not to the panel: cut here, paste in the file
manager of another workspace, or from the right-click menu of a list
([[Context menus]]); copy in the [[metarecord-list panel]] and paste here. A cut is
emptied by its paste, and `clipboard:clear` empties it. It is the global GUI variable
`clipboard` ([[Global GUI variables]]): the [[workspace-info panel]] shows what it
holds.

Deleting sends the entry to the repository's trash, tracked or not, together with its
metarecords, and the [[trash panel]] restores it ([[Sending files to the trash]]).
An entry no repository holds — none is active, or the folder is outside its root —
goes to the desktop's trash, which a file manager restores from
([[The desktop trash]]). Nothing is deleted for good.

!! Right click

A right click moves the cursor to the row, then offers ([[Context menus]]):

* for a tracked row, the metarecord's actions and ''Add to the selection'';
* ''Track'';
* ''Open'' for a directory, the clipboard actions, ''Rename…'', ''Duplicate'', ''Copy full path'', ''Move to trash'';
* ''Ignore “name” here'', ''Ignore *.ext here'' and ''Apply an ignore preset…'', which write on the directory shown ([[Setting ignore patterns]]);
* ''New folder…'', ''New file…''.

On the empty part of the listing: ''Paste'', ''New folder…'', ''New file…''.

!! As a folder picker

Where a form asks for a folder — the root of a repository to create or load in
[[repos panel]] — it opens this panel in the other slot ([[Value picker]]). The right
click then starts with ''Pick this folder'', which confirms without a key.

!! Its variables

|!Variable |!Holds |
|`file-manager:dir` |the directory shown — what the `ignore:*` commands take as their target |
|`file-manager:cursor` |the name of the entry highlighted in it, or `null` |

The two are the panel's ''location'', not a record of it: written by a command, a
script or another panel, the panel goes there — at once when it is on screen, when it
next is otherwise; with no `file-manager:dir`, it opens at the repository root.
`file-manager:reveal` writes them, and so does a folder picker, to start where the form
already points. A write of where the panel already is, or of what it wrote itself,
does nothing ([[Cross-panel selection]]). Nor does a read of the variables that
overlaps one of the panel's own moves: begun before it, it finds where the panel
''was'' — following it sent a double-click into a folder straight back to the
parent — so it is dropped, and the variables re-read once the move's writes are done.

The view settings — the root constraint, hidden files, the activity or operations order — are
not variables: they are the panel's, for the session.
